ise brief on what the meeting appears to require. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-calendar/1.2.4/skills/google-calendar-meeting-prep/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-docs: Connector-first Google Docs creation and editing in local Codex plugin sessions, with direct native create and batchUpdate workflows for simple docs, DOCX-first import for polished deliverables, target-document checks, smart chip and building-block reconstruction, connector-readback verification, and reference routing for formatting, citations, tables, and write-safety. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-drive/0.1.8/skills/google-docs/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-drive: Use connected Google Drive as the single entrypoint for Drive, Docs, Sheets, and Slides work. Use when the user wants to find, fetch, organize, share, export, copy, or delete Drive files, or summarize and edit Google Docs, Google Sheets, and Google Slides through one unified Google Drive plugin. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-drive/0.1.8/skills/google-drive/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-drive-comments: Write, reply to, and resolve Google Drive comments on Docs, Sheets, Slides, and Drive files with evidence-backed location context. Use when the user asks to leave comments, review a file with comments, respond to comment threads, or resolve Drive comments. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-drive/0.1.8/skills/google-drive-comments/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-sheets: Analyze and edit connected Google Sheets with range precision. Use when the user wants to create Google Sheets, find a spreadsheet, inspect tabs or ranges, search rows, plan formulas, create or repair charts, clean or restructure tables, write concise summaries, or make explicit cell-range updates. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-drive/0.1.8/skills/google-sheets/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-slides: Google Slides work for finding, reading, summarizing, creating, importing, template following, visual cleanup, source-deck adaptation, structural repair, and content edits in native Slides decks. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-drive/0.1.8/skills/google-slides/SKILL.md)\n- hardware-check: Avant toute commande ffmpeg/ImageMagick/HandBrake/montage vidéo/traitement d'image lourd ou tout job ML audio-vidéo (VoiceFixer, DeepFilterNet, Resemble-Enhance, Demucs, UVR...), vérifie le matériel (cores P/E, RAM libre EN DIRECT, encodeurs matériels disponibles type VideoToolbox/NVENC) et donne le réglage de parallélisme optimal. Distingue le parallélisme SANS RISQUE à pousser au maximum (ffmpeg encodage matériel, ImageMagick, xargs, tout CPU-local) du parallélisme DANGEREUX (jobs ML/torch — jamais deux en parallèle, garde-fou RAM obligatoire). Utiliser avant un encodage, un remux, un réencodage, un batch d'images, ou dès qu'une tâche va faire tourner le CPU/GPU fort et longtemps. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/skills/hardware-check/SKILL.md)\n- interview-audio: Pipeline audio complet pour les musiques de fond et la voix d'une interview/vidéo. Télécharge une piste (yt-dlp, recherche ou URL) en WAV, applique fade in/out, et normalise — soit en normalisation CLASSIQUE (pic à un dBFS cible, ex -12), soit en LOUDNESS (loudnorm LUFS, ex -28 pour une BGM sous la voix, -16 pour la voix). Sait aussi extraire la piste audio d'un MP4 et lui appliquer une chaîne \"voix podcast\" (coupe-bas, chaleur grave, présence, compression douce, loudnorm -16). Utiliser dès que Matthieu veut préparer des musiques sous une interview, des SFX d'intro avec fades, normaliser des WAV à un niveau, ou traiter une voix en son podcast. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/skills/interview-audio/SKILL.md)\n- kanji-stroke-order: Generate a textbook-style stroke-order diagram (SVG) for any Japanese character (kanji, hiragana, or katakana). Produces one panel per stroke showing completed strokes in black, the current stroke highlighted with a red number and directional arrow at its starting point, and remaining strokes ghosted in light gray. Use this skill whenever the user asks how to write a Japanese character, requests stroke order, asks \"in what order do I draw X\", wants to learn or memorize a kanji, asks to decompose a character into strokes, says \"show me the strokes for X\", mentions 書き順 / kakijun, or shows a stroke-order chart and asks for one for a different character. Trigger even when the user only provides a single character and the intent is implicit from the language-learning context. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/skills/kanji-stroke-order/SKILL.md)\n- kanji-stroke-order-html: Generate a complete standalone HTML study sheet for a Japanese kanji — stroke-order SVG inlined directly into the HTML body, plus a structured template with ON reading, KUN reading, stroke count, radical decomposition, mnemonic, 3-4 examples, and a sentence using the kanji. Produces a single self-contained .html file that opens correctly in any browser AND in Codex app's preview (no external file references). Use this skill whenever Matthieu learns a new kanji during his Japanese study sessions and needs the rich study sheet saved into Memory/Japanese/KanjiProgress/. For raw SVG without HTML wrapper, use the sibling skill `kanji-stroke-order-svg` instead. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/skills/kanji-stroke-order-html/SKILL.md)\n- kanji-stroke-order-svg: Generate a standalone textbook-style stroke-order SVG for any Japanese character (kanji, hiragana, or katakana). Produces one panel per stroke — completed strokes in black, current stroke highlighted with red number and directional arrow, remaining strokes ghosted in light gray. Use this skill when the user wants ONLY the stroke-order diagram as a raw SVG (no HTML wrapper, no metadata). For the full HTML kanji study sheet with ON/KUN/mnemonic/examples bundled in, use the sibling skill `kanji-stroke-order-html` instead. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/skills/kanji-stroke-order-svg/SKILL.md)\n- masterclass-builder: Use this skill to design rigorous, deep masterclasses and multi-module curricula (roughly 90 minutes per module, extensible to 15-20h) that build durable understanding and autonomous capability, not passive \"AI slop.\" Trigger this whenever the user wants to create a masterclass, a course, a deep curriculum, a structured learning program, progressive exercises on a topic, a study plan, or wants to genuinely LEARN a domain (not just get a one-shot answer), even if they do not use the word \"course.\" Covers learner profiling, 80/20 syllabus design, mechanism-level explanation (why before how), scaffolded progressive exercises, active recall, decision-forcing outputs, multi-agent adversarially verified research, fact verification, and an anti-slop self-audit. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/skills/masterclass-builder/SKILL.md)\n- notion:notion-knowledge-capture: Capture conversations and decisions into structured Notion pages; use when turning chats/notes into wiki entries, how-tos, decisions, or FAQs with proper linking. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/notion/0.1.7/skills/notion-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md)\n- notion:notion-meeting-intelligence: Prepare meeting materials with Notion context and supplemental research; use when gathering context, drafting agendas/pre-reads, and tailoring materials to attendees. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/notion/0.1.7/skills/notion-meeting-intelligence/SKILL.md)\n- notion:notion-research-documentation: Research across Notion and synthesize into structured documentation; use when gathering info from multiple Notion sources to produce briefs, comparisons, or reports with citations. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/notion/0.1.7/skills/notion-research-documentation/SKILL.md)\n- notion:notion-spec-to-implementation: Turn Notion specs into implementation plans, tasks, and progress tracking; use when implementing PRDs/feature specs and creating Notion plans + tasks from them. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/notion/0.1.7/skills/notion-spec-to-implementation/SKILL.md)\n- pdf:pdf: Read, create, inspect, render, and verify PDF files where visual layout matters. Use Poppler rendering plus Python tools such as reportlab, pdfplumber, and pypdf for generation and extraction. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/pdf/26.709.11516/skills/pdf/SKILL.md)\n- presentations:Presentations: Create or edit PowerPoint or Google Slides decks (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/presentations/26.709.11516/skills/presentations/SKILL.md)\n- reduce-echo: Répare un enregistrement audio/vidéo (appel, interview, visio) qui souffre d'écho ou de réverbération causés par une double capture audio — typiquement un micro qui recapte le son sorti des enceintes, ou deux chemins audio mixés dans la même piste avec un délai qui DÉRIVE dans le temps (ex 30ms au début, 50ms une heure plus tard). Chaîne complète en plusieurs passes IA + DSP, jamais une seule : filtre soustractif adaptatif par blocs (mesure et suit le délai qui dérive), VoiceFixer (régénération générative de la voix, efface l'écho qu'un simple filtre ne peut pas), réparation automatique des passages que les modèles génératifs avalent/gatent (fuite de mots sinon), DeepFilterNet3 (débruitage), et polish podcast final (EQ voix grave, compression douce, loudnorm -16 LUFS en 2 passes linéaires). Traite par chunks séquentiels avec garde mémoire pour ne jamais saturer la RAM. Utiliser quand Matthieu dit qu'un enregistrement a de l'écho, de la réverbération, un son \"d'église\", une voix qui résonne, un double audio... (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/skills/reduce-echo/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-building: Use Sites to build websites, including landing pages, portfolios, dashboards, portals, trackers, hubs, and internal tools. Always use Sites when the project contains `.openai/hosting.json`. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled/sites/0.1.27/skills/sites-building/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-hosting: Host websites with Sites. Always use after `sites-building`, and use for website publishing, deployment, hosting management, or projects containing `.openai/hosting.json`. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled/sites/0.1.27/skills/sites-hosting/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:Spreadsheets: Create, edit, analyze, and verify standalone spreadsheet files or Google Sheets-ready workbooks, including .xlsx, .xls, .csv, and .tsv. Do not use for live controlling Microsoft Excel app or a live Excel session. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/spreadsheets/26.709.11516/skills/spreadsheets/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:excel-live-control: Control an open or active Microsoft Excel workbook through the ChatGPT add-in or connected session. Use when the user tags the Microsoft Excel app in Codex or follows up on an established live Excel task. Do not use for standalone spreadsheet files or Google Sheets. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/spreadsheets/26.709.11516/skills/excel-live-control/SKILL.md)\n- srt-yt-anime: Extrait le sous-titre d'un ou plusieurs fichiers .mkv (anime fansub, ASS/SSA le plus souvent) et produit un .srt en texte brut, sans balises <font>/<b>, prêt à uploader dans YouTube Studio. YouTube Studio n'interprète pas les balises de style ASS/SRT et les affiche telles quelles à l'écran si on ne les retire pas. Utiliser dès que Matthieu veut des sous-titres SRT propres pour YouTube depuis un mkv, un épisode, ou une saison entière. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/skills/srt-yt-anime/SKILL.md)\n- template-creator:template-creator: Create or update a reusable personal Codex artifact-template skill. Use when the user invokes $template-creator or asks in natural language to create a template using, from, or based on an attached Word document, PowerPoint presentation, or Excel workbook, or explicitly asks to edit or update a passed artifact-template skill. Do not use for one-off artifact creation from an existing template. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/template-creator/26.709.11516/skills/template-creator/SKILL.md)\n- think-of-everything: Run a systematic impact and premortem pass on any decision or change in any domain — code, architecture, product, business, life/admin, travel, purchases, health, learning, art/3D/creative. Reads the request four ways (literal, inverse, adjacent, reframed), verifies the real facts instead of guessing from memory (grep the codebase, read the actual documents and numbers, search official sources), checks a 12-axis impact surface (existing state, conflicts, limits and deadlines, security/legal, partial failure, backward compatibility, scale, recurring cost, observability, edge cases, checks, reversibility), runs a domain-specific premortem, then delivers at most 5 ranked risks with exact proof and a concrete verification each, ending in a GO / NO-GO verdict at paid-specialist precision, never generic. Use whenever the user says \"pense à tout\", \"think of everything\", \"qu'est-ce que j'ai oublié\", \"what am I missing\", asks what a change or decision might break, or wants a premortem, dependency check, or impact a... (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/skills/think-of-everything/SKILL.md)\n- visualize:visualize: Create visualizations and interactive tools in conversation. Use when asked to show how something works, make simulators or labs, maps, plots, charts or graphs, comparisons, scenarios, adjustable inputs, and exploration. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled/visualize/1.0.11/skills/visualize/SKILL.md)\n- ytb-dlp: Télécharger des vidéos, pistes audio, sous-titres ou métadonnées depuis YouTube et les nombreux sites pris en charge par yt-dlp. Utiliser quand l'ut